---
title: Fort Guacamole
cookTime: 20 minutes
totalTime: 20 minutes
source: The Fort, Denver, CO
tags: Appetizer
---

Place the @avocados{3}(ripe, pitted and peeled), @green chiles{2%oz}(minced), @jalepeno{1/2}(minced),
@lime juice{1/4%cup}, and @salt{1/2%tsp} in a large bowl.
Mash the avocados with a fork or potato masher, leaving small lumps.

Gently fold in the @tomato{1}(large, seeded and diced), @white onion{1/2}(diced),
and @cilantro leaves{1/4%cup}(minced, without stems).

Taste, and add more lime juice if desired.
The guacamole should be spicy, so add more heat as your taste dictates. 

Serve with tortilla chips.
